---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host, liability`} description="Legal notice of UK Work Rights: publisher Radif Partners, publication director, hosting provider, purpose of the calculators, limits of liability, intellectual property and governing law." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004 on confidence in the digital economy, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Hosting provider</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
    <p>The site offers free calculators and guides on statutory employment rights in the United Kingdom (redundancy pay, notice, holiday, family pay and sick pay). Results are estimates of the <strong>statutory minimum</strong> from the facts you enter. They are not legal advice and do not bind your employer, HMRC or an employment or industrial tribunal. The site is independent and has no link with GOV.UK, HMRC, Acas, nidirect or the Labour Relations Agency. Method and limits: <a href={route('method', lang)}>method</a>.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Figures are re-read at their sources at each change in the law and the calculations are covered by automated tests, without any guarantee that no error remains. The publisher cannot be held liable for a decision taken on the sole basis of a result. Errors can be reported through the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>Texts, graphics and code belong to the publisher; short quotations with a link to the page are welcome. Crown copyright material and legislation quoted from legislation.gov.uk and GOV.UK are reused under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>.</p>
    <h2>Embedding</h2><p>The redundancy pay calculator can be embedded free of charge with the credit link kept visible: <a href={route('widget', lang)}>embed page</a>.</p>
    <h2>Personal data</h2><p>What you type stays in your browser: see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, with the page address and the reason.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law. Failing an amicable solution, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without prejudice to the mandatory rules protecting consumers in their country of residence. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
